WEBVTT

00:00.859 --> 00:02.940
- [Instructor] So we have this circle

00:02.940 --> 00:03.870
called circle O,

00:03.870 --> 00:05.660
based on the point at its center,

00:05.660 --> 00:07.860
and we have the segment OD,

00:07.860 --> 00:10.080
and we're told that segment OD,

00:10.080 --> 00:12.470
is a radius of circle O, fair enough.

00:12.470 --> 00:13.370
We're also told

00:13.370 --> 00:17.520
that segment OD is
perpendicular to this chord

00:17.520 --> 00:20.540
to chord AC, or two segment AC.

00:20.540 --> 00:25.023
And what we wanna prove is
that segment OD bisects AC.

00:26.080 --> 00:27.660
So another way to think about it,

00:27.660 --> 00:31.120
it intersects AC at AC's midpoint.

00:31.120 --> 00:34.710
So pause this video and see if
you can have a go with that.

00:34.710 --> 00:36.680
All right, now let's go
through this together.

00:36.680 --> 00:38.010
And the way that I'm going to do this,

00:38.010 --> 00:40.990
is by establishing two
congruent triangles.

00:40.990 --> 00:42.670
And let me draw these triangles.

00:42.670 --> 00:46.730
So I'm gonna draw one
radius going from O to C

00:46.730 --> 00:51.260
and another from A to O.

00:51.260 --> 00:56.200
Now we know that the
length AO is equal to OC

01:01.490 --> 01:06.490
because AO and OC, both radii.

01:12.420 --> 01:15.610
In a circle, the length of
the radius does not change.

01:15.610 --> 01:19.150
So I can put that right over there.

01:19.150 --> 01:21.910
And then we also know that OM

01:21.910 --> 01:23.810
is going to be congruent to itself,

01:23.810 --> 01:26.440
it's a side in both of these triangles.

01:26.440 --> 01:28.416
So let me just write it this way.

01:28.416 --> 01:33.416
OM is going to be congruent to OM

01:36.310 --> 01:38.105
and this is reflexivity.

01:38.105 --> 01:42.710
Reflexivity kind of obvious.

01:42.710 --> 01:44.320
It's going to be equal to itself,

01:44.320 --> 01:46.140
it's going to be congruent to itself.

01:46.140 --> 01:47.630
So you have it just like that.

01:47.630 --> 01:49.270
And now we have two right triangles.

01:49.270 --> 01:50.590
How do I know they're right triangles?

01:50.590 --> 01:51.780
Well, they told us

01:51.780 --> 01:55.520
that segment OD is
perpendicular to segment AC

01:55.520 --> 01:58.290
and our assumptions in our given.

01:58.290 --> 02:00.130
Now if you just had two triangles,

02:00.130 --> 02:03.310
that had two pairs of congruent sides

02:03.310 --> 02:06.960
that is not enough to establish
congruency of the triangles.

02:06.960 --> 02:09.090
But if you're dealing
with two right triangles,

02:09.090 --> 02:10.660
then it is enough.

02:10.660 --> 02:12.470
And there's two ways to think about it.

02:12.470 --> 02:17.180
We had thought about the RSH postulate

02:17.180 --> 02:19.070
where if you have a right triangle

02:19.070 --> 02:20.300
or two right triangles,

02:20.300 --> 02:21.880
you have a pair of sides are congruent,

02:21.880 --> 02:24.250
a pair and the hypothesis are congruent

02:24.250 --> 02:26.920
that means that the two
triangles are congruent.

02:26.920 --> 02:28.010
But another way to think about it,

02:28.010 --> 02:30.580
which is a little bit of common sense is

02:30.580 --> 02:32.150
using the Pythagorean theorem.

02:32.150 --> 02:34.100
If you know two sides of a right triangle,

02:34.100 --> 02:35.400
the Pythagorean theorem would tell us

02:35.400 --> 02:38.680
that you could determine
what the other side is.

02:38.680 --> 02:40.690
And so what we could say is

02:40.690 --> 02:42.130
and let's just use RSH for now,

02:42.130 --> 02:45.080
but you could also say we can
use the Pythagorean theorem

02:45.080 --> 02:50.080
to establish that AM is
going to be congruent to MC,

02:50.390 --> 02:51.950
but let me just write it this way.

02:51.950 --> 02:55.193
I will write that triangle,

02:56.079 --> 03:01.079
AMO is congruent to triangle CMO by RSH.

03:06.350 --> 03:07.870
And if the triangles are congruent

03:07.870 --> 03:10.640
then the corresponding
sides must be congruent.

03:10.640 --> 03:14.443
So, therefore, we know that AM,

03:15.894 --> 03:19.850
AM, segment AM is going to be,

03:19.850 --> 03:21.180
I'm having trouble writing congruent

03:21.180 --> 03:23.943
is going to be congruent to segment CM,

03:26.670 --> 03:31.590
that these are going to
have the same measure.

03:31.590 --> 03:33.160
And if they have the same measure,

03:33.160 --> 03:37.750
we have just shown that
M is the midpoint of AC

03:37.750 --> 03:40.210
or that OD bisects AC.

03:40.210 --> 03:41.210
So, let me just write it that way.

03:41.210 --> 03:43.550
Therefore, OD bisects AC.

03:48.075 --> 03:52.023
Segment OD bisects
segment AC and we're done.
